{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch79LCBVxZJhtswKN9GAc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A6wABUA6HDAaKy94ac3jZh","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/audit_log.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":92964,"cache_read_input_tokens":4473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":92964},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"178172ab-278a-4318-ba3b-1534bf22937a","uuid":"96ec768f-d4a3-4e53-98ec-73623a606d5a","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:17:20.249Z","request_id":"req_011Ch79LBu94Z4S86pxnBfa1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01A6wABUA6HDAaKy94ac3jZh":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/audit_log.py"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6wABUA6HDAaKy94ac3jZh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"PostToolUse Agent audit log — Python single-file hook with rotation.\n3\t\n4\tPort of `.claude/scripts/audit-log.sh` to stdlib Python. Bash version\n5\tremains untouched until A.4 flips settings.json to the Python shim.\n6\t\n7\t## Schema\n8\t\n9\tIdentical to AUDIT-LOG-SCHEMA.md with these additions:\n10\t\n11\t- `hook_duration_ms` (integer) — wallclock duration of the hook itself,\n12\t  measured at end of processing. Enables `audit-query.py stats --latency`\n13\t  analysis in Sprint 3 without re-instrumenting the hooks.\n14\t\n15\tPLAN-020 Phase 0 item 1 (audit-log v2.7 schema bump — ADDITIVE):\n16\t\n17\t- `usage_metadata` (object|null) — Anthropic API usage_metadata\n18\t  passthrough. Keys: `cache_creation_input_tokens`,\n19\t  `cache_read_input_tokens`, `uncached_input_tokens`, `output_tokens`,\n20\t  `thinking_tokens`. Each is integer or null. Captured per spawn for\n21\t  cache-coverage analysis (PLAN-020 §6 sub-target measurement).\n22\t- `cache_coverage_bps` (int|null) — derived metric in integer\n23\t  basis-points (ratio × 10000, clamped [0, 10000]):\n24\t  `cache_read / (cache_read + cache_creation + uncached)`. Null if\n25\t  totals unavailable. PLAN-020 §6 acceptance: P50 +10pp vs Phase 0\n26\t  baseline. PLAN-118 WS-E (S181): replaced the legacy `cache_coverage`\n27\t  float — floats break the HMAC-covered payload (canonical_json\n28\t  no-float invariant). The derivation helper still returns the float\n29\t  ratio; the producer converts to bps before the entry dict.\n30\t- `rail` (string|null) — spawn dispatch rail: `\"native\"` |\n31\t  `\"custom\"` | null (legacy / unknown). Discriminator for ADR-050\n32\t  dual-rail A/B harness. PLAN-019 emitters (pre-PLAN-020) emit null;\n33\t  PLAN-020 Phase 1+ emitters set the value.\n34\t\n35\tAll three fields are ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore them safely.\n36\t\n37\tPLAN-021 ADR-052 (audit-log v2.8 schema bump — ADDITIVE):\n38\t\n39\t- `model` (string|null) — Claude model ID used for the spawn. Values\n40\t  are canonical Anthropic IDs of the CURRENT fleet (e.g.\n41\t  `\"claude-fable-5\"`, `\"claude-opus-5\"`, `\"claude-sonnet-5\"`,\n42\t  `\"claude-haiku-4-5\"`; N-1 ids like `\"claude-opus-4-8\"` remain valid\n43\t  in replay), or null if unknown. Captured from `tool_response.model`\n44\t  when Anthropic API\n45\t  emits it, else null. Enables forensic correlation: if a\n46\t  Sonnet-routed review misses a bug, the audit log proves which\n47\t  model made the decision.\n48\t\n49\tField is ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore; pre-v2.8 emitters emit\n50\tnull.\n51\t\n52\tPLAN-065 Phase 1 (audit-log v2.15 — extract_skill 3-path matrix):\n53\t\n54\t- `extract_skill()` ports the validated 3-path logic from\n55\t  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` (58 tests, ReDoS-hardened) inline\n56\t  into the hook so audit-log emit covers Format-A inline / Format-B\n57\t  reference / Format-C `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Restores\n58\t  observability of `skill=<name>` post-ADR-082 mitigated dispatch +\n59\t  Format-B SKILL REFERENCE default flip. Pre-Phase 1 baseline: 24/24\n60\t  agent_spawn rows had `skill=\"unknown\"` (100% loss). Target ≤10%\n61\t  unknown in 30d post-merge.\n62\t\n63\t  Sec MF-7 hardening: NFKC normalize, NUL byte denied, length cap\n64\t  256 chars on captured group, path traversal denied (the captured\n65\t  group grammar excludes `/` `..` `\\\\`), regex bounded quantifiers\n66\t  `{0,255}` (no nested unbounded alternation — ReDoS-safe).\n67\t\n68\tPLAN-079 (extract_skill Path D — canonical archetype mapping):\n69\t\n70\t- Path D added to `extract_skill()` as a TAIL fallback (after Paths\n71\t  A/B/C miss). Maps the 5 canonical archetypes — `code-reviewer`,\n72\t  `security-engineer`, `qa-architect`, `performance-engineer`,\n73\t  `devops` — to their canonical skill names per ADR-051 (sub-agents\n74\t  load skills via `.claude/agents/<name>.md` reference, not inline).\n75\t  Closes the observability gap S87/S88 surfaced (20/26 unknown\n76\t  agent_spawn rows on canonical-archetype dispatches without\n77\t  inline SKILL CONTENT).\n78\t\n79\t  Backwards compat: signature changed from `extract_skill(prompt)`\n80\t  to `extract_skill(prompt, subagent_type=\"\")` — default arg\n81\t  preserves all single-arg callers. Frozen mapping constant\n82\t  `_ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL` (no runtime I/O); drift-detector test\n83\t  (`test_audit_log_path_d.py`) asserts the table matches the\n84\t  \"Loads <skill> skill via reference\" phrase in each\n85\t  `.claude/agents/<archetype>.md` description frontmatter.\n86\t\n87\t  Sec MF-7 defense-in-depth: `subagent_type` is normalized via\n88\t  `strip().lower()` (case-fold mirrors `check_agent_spawn.py:204`\n89\t  archetype-routing precedent), then validated POST-NORMALIZE\n90\t  against `_ARCHETYPE_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z][a-z0-9\\\\-]{0,63}$` with\n91\t  `.fullmatch`). A raw-length pre-bound (`len > 80`) caps\n92\t  hot-path allocation. Rejected silently: slash, dot-traversal,\n93\t  NUL, unicode, oversize, non-string. Uppercase is INTENTIONALLY\n94\t  case-folded (NOT rejected) — matches Agent-tool emitter\n95\t  flexibility for the routing layer.\n96\t\n97\t## Rotation\n98\t\n99\tNEW in Sprint 2: monthly rotation by size threshold.\n100\t\n101\tBefore writing, if `audit-log.jsonl` exists and its size > ROTATE_AT_BYTES\n102\t(default 10 MB), rename to `audit-log-YYYY-MM.jsonl` (current month) and\n103\tstart a fresh file. If the monthly file already exists (second rotation\n104\tin the same month), append `-1`, `-2`, etc.\n105\t\n106\tThe rotation rename happens UNDER the lock so a concurrent writer can't\n107\tappend to a file that's about to be moved.\n108\t\n109\t## Safety properties\n110\t\n111\t1. Fail-open: any exception writes a breadcrumb to `audit-log.errors`\n112\t   and exits 0. The user's session MUST NOT be blocked by this hook.\n113\t2. Silent on stdout: composable with the reminder hook.\n114\t3. Env-var overrides (`CEO_AUDIT_LOG_*`) for testability.\n115\t4. Redaction via `_lib.redact` (property-tested).\n116\t5. Locking via `_lib.filelock` (fcntl.flock).\n117\t\n118\t## Decomposition candidates\n119\t\n120\tThis module has accreted ~7 responsibilities across PLAN-019..PLAN-079.\n121\tTracked decomposition targets for PLAN-085+ readers (NO extraction in\n122\tPLAN-087 — doc-only surface; per `F-A-CR-D0016` P2 + PLAN-084 evolution\n123\troadmap):\n124\t\n125\t- **Path A — `extract_skill()` extraction.** Lines for the 3-path\n126\t  matrix (Format-A inline / Format-B reference / Format-C ``## SKILL\n127\t  CONTENT`` block) plus Path D canonical archetype map are a\n128\t  self-contained extraction target. Candidate destination:\n129\t  `_lib/skill_extract.py` (already exists as the standalone module\n130\t  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` — the in-hook copy duplicates\n131\t  logic kept inline so audit-log emit covers the dispatch hot path\n132\t  without subprocess fork). Extraction would centralize the regex\n133\t  contract; trade-off is per-spawn import cost.\n134\t- **Path B — `usage_metadata` / `cache_coverage_bps` derivation.** The\n135\t  v2.7 / v2.8 schema bump logic (lines ~15-43 in this docstring) is\n136\t  arithmetic on `tool_response`. Candidate destination:\n137\t  `_lib/usage_metadata.py` (mirrors `_lib/tokens.py` adapter pattern).\n138\t- **Path C — HMAC chain integration.** The audit-chain HMAC writer\n139\t  is currently invoked from this hook's main path. Candidate\n140\t  destination: `_lib/audit_hmac.py` (already exists as the HMAC\n141\t  verifier — the writer-side wrapper would mirror the\n142\t  ``verify_chain()`` API). Extraction unblocks the two-writer\n143\t  asymmetry surfaced as PLAN-084 finding C.1.\n144\t- **Path D — Orchestrator split.** The PostToolUse dispatch logic\n145\t  (rotation + redaction + emit + HMAC + breadcrumb fallback) is the\n146\t  remaining \"orchestrator\" after Paths A/B/C peel off. Candidate\n147\t  destination: keep `audit_log.py` as a ~150-line thin shim that\n148\t  delegates to the four `_lib/*` modules.\n149\t\n150\tEach Path is sized to one PLAN-08x phase; extraction order is\n151\tA → C → B → D (Path C unblocks the two-writer fix, so it lands\n152\tahead of B/D).\n153\t\"\"\"\n154\t\n155\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n156\t\n157\timport getpass\n158\timport json\n159\timport os\n160\timport re\n161\timport stat\n162\timport sys\n163\timport time\n164\timport unicodedata\n165\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n166\tfrom pathlib import Path\n167\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n168\t\n169\t# Make `.claude/hooks/` importable so `_lib` resolves.\n170\t_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n171\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n172\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n173\t\n174\tfrom _lib import contract as _contract  # noqa: E402\n175\tfrom _lib import payload as _payload  # noqa: E402  (response_kind helper)\n176\tfrom _lib import redact as _redact  # noqa: E402\n177\tfrom _lib import tokens as _tokens  # noqa: E402  (PLAN-006 Phase 5b / ADR-016)\n178\tfrom _lib.adapters import claude as _claude_adapter  # noqa: E402\n179\tfrom _lib.filelock import FileLock, FileLockTimeout  # noqa: E402\n180\ttry:\n181\t    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402  # PLAN-182 W1 single resolver\n182\texcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover — partial upgrade: hook stays FAIL-OPEN (rail r1 P1-4)\n183\t    _rp = None  # type: ignore[assignment]\n184\t\n185\t\n186\tdef _rp_state_dir():\n187\t    \"\"\"Resolver com fallback de partial-upgrade (arquivo novo ausente).\n188\t\n189\t    Fail-open: o hook NUNCA crasha por falta do resolvedor; degrada ao\n190\t    comportamento legado com aviso em stderr.\n191\t    \"\"\"\n192\t    if _rp is not None:\n193\t        return _rp.runtime_state_dir()\n194\t    import sys as _s  # pragma: no cover — partial-upgrade fallback\n195\t    _s.stderr.write(\"# hook: _lib/runtime_paths ausente — fallback legado (partial upgrade)\\n\")  # pragma: no cover\n196\t    from pathlib import Path as _P  # pragma: no cover\n197\t    import os as _o  # pragma: no cover\n198\t    _h = _o.environ.get(\"HOME\") or str(_P.home())  # pragma: no cover\n199\t    return _P(_h) / \".claude\" / \"projects\" / \"ceo-orchestration\"  # rp-allow: partial-upgrade-fallback  # pragma: no cover\n200\t\n201\t\n202\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n203\t# Constants\n204\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n205\t\n206\t# Default rotation threshold: 10 MB. Overridable via CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES.\n207\tDEFAULT_ROTATE_AT_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n208\t\n209\t# PLAN-065 Phase 1 — Sec MF-7 input bounds.\n210\t# Cap inputs at 1 MiB to keep the regex engine in linear-time territory.\n211\t# Plans / prompts beyond this size are extreme outliers; rejecting them is\n212\t# preferred over feeding pathological input to the regex engine.\n213\t_MAX_INPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024  # 1 MiB hard cap\n214\t_MAX_INPUT_BYTES = _MAX_INPUT_CHARS\n215\t\n216\t# Skill-name max length (PLAN-065 §4.1 fixture spec — 256-char cap).\n217\t_MAX_SKILL_NAME_CHARS = 256\n218\t\n219\t# Allowed skill-name character class — ``[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]*`` anchored.\n220\t# Used as defense-in-depth re-validation post-extract.\n221\t_SKILL_NAME_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]*$\")\n222\t\n223\t# PLAN-065 Phase 1 — 3-path SKILL extraction matrix.\n224\t#\n225\t# Path A — Format-A inline. Line-anchored ``^SKILL: <name>$``. Bounded\n226\t# {0,255} quantifier on the captured group, no nested unbounded alternation\n227\t# (ReDoS-safe). Mirrors the validated grammar in extract-skill.py:_PATH_A_RE.\n228\t_SKILL_PATH_A_RE = re.compile(\n229\t    r\"(?m)^SKILL:[ \\t]+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,255})\\s*$\",\n230\t)\n231\t\n232\t# Path B — Format-B reference (mitigated dispatch + SKILL REFERENCE default).\n233\t#   @.claude/skills/core/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>\n234\t#   @.claude/skills/frontend/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>\n235\t#   @.claude/skills/domains/<domain>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>\n236\t# Captured group is the skill <name> path-segment, not the domain.\n237\t_SKILL_PATH_B_RE = re.compile(\n238\t    r\"(?m)^@\\.claude/skills/\"\n239\t    r\"(?:core|frontend|domains/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,63}/skills)\"\n240\t    r\"/([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,255})/SKILL\\.md\"\n241\t    r\"\\s+sha256=[0-9a-f]{64}\\s*$\",\n242\t)\n243\t\n244\t# Path C — `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Used when neither Format-A\n245\t# nor Format-B was emitted (legacy / third-party adapter surface). The block\n246\t# heading has a sibling `SKILL LOADED: <name>` annotation.\n247\t_SKILL_PATH_C_HEADER_RE = re.compile(\n248\t    r\"(?m)^##[ \\t]+SKILL[ \\t]+CONTENT\\b\",\n249\t)\n250\t_SKILL_PATH_C_LOADED_RE = re.compile(\n251\t    r\"(?m)^SKILL[ \\t]+LOADED:[ \\t]+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,255})\\s*$\",\n252\t)\n253\t\n254\t# PLAN-079 Path D — canonical archetype subagent_type → skill mapping.\n255\t#\n256\t# Sub-agent dispatches via ``Agent({subagent_type:\"<archetype>\"})`` load\n257\t# their persona + skill via ``.claude/agents/<archetype>.md`` reference\n258\t# per ADR-051 (PLAN-020). When the spawn prompt does NOT carry an\n259\t# explicit Format-A/B/C SKILL envelope, Paths A-C all miss and the\n260\t# pre-PLAN-079 behavior recorded ``skill=\"unknown\"``. This frozen map\n261\t# closes the observability gap by mapping the 5 canonical archetypes\n262\t# to their loaded skill name. Frozen baseline pattern (mirrors\n263\t# ``_FROZEN_BASELINE`` in tier_policy/_constants.py) — no runtime I/O\n264\t# against agent files; drift-detector test asserts the table matches\n265\t# the \"Loads <skill> skill via reference\" phrase in each\n266\t# ``.claude/agents/<archetype>.md`` description frontmatter.\n267\t_ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL: Dict[str, str] = {\n268\t    \"code-reviewer\": \"code-review-checklist\",\n269\t    \"security-engineer\": \"security-and-auth\",\n270\t    \"qa-architect\": \"testing-strategy\",\n271\t    \"performance-engineer\": \"performance-engineering\",\n272\t    \"devops\": \"devops-ci-cd\",\n273\t    # PLAN-106 Wave B.2 (H3 fix) — additional archetypes recorded as\n274\t    # `unknown` in 24h rolling because Path D lookup missed them. The\n275\t    # canonical skill name on the right-hand side must match a real\n276\t    # `.claude/skills/**/<name>/SKILL.md`. If the file is absent at\n277\t    # adopter time the map still resolves the string; the downstream\n278\t    # consumer is `audit_log.py:extract_skill()` Path D tail which\n279\t    # records the string verbatim — no I/O.\n280\t    \"identity-trust-architect\": \"identity-and-trust-architecture\",\n281\t    \"incident-commander\": \"incident-management\",\n282\t    \"llm-finops-architect\": \"llm-routing-and-finops\",\n283\t    \"threat-detection-engineer\": \"security-and-auth\",\n284\t}\n285\t\n286\t# Defense-in-depth charset for ``subagent_type`` AFTER `strip().lower()`\n287\t# normalize (untrusted spawn-payload field). Bounded {0,63} quantifier —\n288\t# no nested unbounded alternation (ReDoS-safe). Validated POST-NORMALIZE\n289\t# via `.fullmatch` — uppercase input is case-folded BEFORE this check\n290\t# (intentional, mirrors check_agent_spawn.py:204). Rejects (post-normalize):\n291\t# dot-traversal `..`, slashes, NUL, unicode, oversize.\n292\t_ARCHETYPE_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z][a-z0-9\\-]{0,63}$\")\n293\t\n294\t# Governance markers in the prompt\n295\t_PROFILE_RE = re.compile(r\"^(## AGENT PROFILE|## PERSONA|PERSONA:)\", re.MULTILINE)\n296\t_FILE_ASSIGNMENT_RE = re.compile(r\"^## FILE ASSIGNMENT\", re.MULTILINE)\n297\t\n298\t\n299\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n300\t# Path resolution\n301\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n302\t\n303\t\n304\t\n305\t# PLAN-074 Wave 1c provenance — see docs/PLAN-086-adr-052-role-extension.md\n306\t# Runtime declarations are split into installable, inspectable library files.\n307\t# They execute once in this facade dictionary so private names, mutable globals\n308\t# and monkeypatch seams retain the historical lookup behavior.\n309\tfrom pathlib import Path as _FacadePath\n310\t\n311\t_PARTS = (\n312\t    \"paths_skills\", \"entries_usage\", \"rotation_storage\", \"adapters_runtime\",\n313\t)\n314\t# Entry payload emits \"skill\" key via entries_usage.py\n315\t_FACADE_DOC = __doc__\n316\t\n317\tdef _install_parts() -> None:\n318\t    \"\"\"Execute ordered real source fragments in this module namespace.\"\"\"\n319\t    namespace = globals()\n320\t    directory = _FacadePath(__file__).resolve().parent / \"_lib\" / \"_audit_log_parts\"\n321\t    for part_name in _PARTS:\n322\t        part_path = directory / (part_name + \".py\")\n323\t        source = part_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n324\t        exec(compile(source, str(part_path), \"exec\"), namespace, namespace)\n325\t\n326\t\n327\t_install_parts()\n328\t__doc__ = _FACADE_DOC\n329\tdel _install_parts, _FacadePath, _FACADE_DOC\n330\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"178172ab-278a-4318-ba3b-1534bf22937a","uuid":"b765964f-f085-41f5-8af8-617a0e1921da","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:17:20.280Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/audit_log.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"PostToolUse Agent audit log — Python single-file hook with rotation.\n\nPort of `.claude/scripts/audit-log.sh` to stdlib Python. Bash version\nremains untouched until A.4 flips settings.json to the Python shim.\n\n## Schema\n\nIdentical to AUDIT-LOG-SCHEMA.md with these additions:\n\n- `hook_duration_ms` (integer) — wallclock duration of the hook itself,\n  measured at end of processing. Enables `audit-query.py stats --latency`\n  analysis in Sprint 3 without re-instrumenting the hooks.\n\nPLAN-020 Phase 0 item 1 (audit-log v2.7 schema bump — ADDITIVE):\n\n- `usage_metadata` (object|null) — Anthropic API usage_metadata\n  passthrough. Keys: `cache_creation_input_tokens`,\n  `cache_read_input_tokens`, `uncached_input_tokens`, `output_tokens`,\n  `thinking_tokens`. Each is integer or null. Captured per spawn for\n  cache-coverage analysis (PLAN-020 §6 sub-target measurement).\n- `cache_coverage_bps` (int|null) — derived metric in integer\n  basis-points (ratio × 10000, clamped [0, 10000]):\n  `cache_read / (cache_read + cache_creation + uncached)`. Null if\n  totals unavailable. PLAN-020 §6 acceptance: P50 +10pp vs Phase 0\n  baseline. PLAN-118 WS-E (S181): replaced the legacy `cache_coverage`\n  float — floats break the HMAC-covered payload (canonical_json\n  no-float invariant). The derivation helper still returns the float\n  ratio; the producer converts to bps before the entry dict.\n- `rail` (string|null) — spawn dispatch rail: `\"native\"` |\n  `\"custom\"` | null (legacy / unknown). Discriminator for ADR-050\n  dual-rail A/B harness. PLAN-019 emitters (pre-PLAN-020) emit null;\n  PLAN-020 Phase 1+ emitters set the value.\n\nAll three fields are ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore them safely.\n\nPLAN-021 ADR-052 (audit-log v2.8 schema bump — ADDITIVE):\n\n- `model` (string|null) — Claude model ID used for the spawn. Values\n  are canonical Anthropic IDs of the CURRENT fleet (e.g.\n  `\"claude-fable-5\"`, `\"claude-opus-5\"`, `\"claude-sonnet-5\"`,\n  `\"claude-haiku-4-5\"`; N-1 ids like `\"claude-opus-4-8\"` remain valid\n  in replay), or null if unknown. Captured from `tool_response.model`\n  when Anthropic API\n  emits it, else null. Enables forensic correlation: if a\n  Sonnet-routed review misses a bug, the audit log proves which\n  model made the decision.\n\nField is ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore; pre-v2.8 emitters emit\nnull.\n\nPLAN-065 Phase 1 (audit-log v2.15 — extract_skill 3-path matrix):\n\n- `extract_skill()` ports the validated 3-path logic from\n  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` (58 tests, ReDoS-hardened) inline\n  into the hook so audit-log emit covers Format-A inline / Format-B\n  reference / Format-C `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Restores\n  observability of `skill=<name>` post-ADR-082 mitigated dispatch +\n  Format-B SKILL REFERENCE default flip. Pre-Phase 1 baseline: 24/24\n  agent_spawn rows had `skill=\"unknown\"` (100% loss). Target ≤10%\n  unknown in 30d post-merge.\n\n  Sec MF-7 hardening: NFKC normalize, NUL byte denied, length cap\n  256 chars on captured group, path traversal denied (the captured\n  group grammar excludes `/` `..` `\\\\`), regex bounded quantifiers\n  `{0,255}` (no nested unbounded alternation — ReDoS-safe).\n\nPLAN-079 (extract_skill Path D — canonical archetype mapping):\n\n- Path D added to `extract_skill()` as a TAIL fallback (after Paths\n  A/B/C miss). Maps the 5 canonical archetypes — `code-reviewer`,\n  `security-engineer`, `qa-architect`, `performance-engineer`,\n  `devops` — to their canonical skill names per ADR-051 (sub-agents\n  load skills via `.claude/agents/<name>.md` reference, not inline).\n  Closes the observability gap S87/S88 surfaced (20/26 unknown\n  agent_spawn rows on canonical-archetype dispatches without\n  inline SKILL CONTENT).\n\n  Backwards compat: signature changed from `extract_skill(prompt)`\n  to `extract_skill(prompt, subagent_type=\"\")` — default arg\n  preserves all single-arg callers. Frozen mapping constant\n  `_ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL` (no runtime I/O); drift-detector test\n  (`test_audit_log_path_d.py`) asserts the table matches the\n  \"Loads <skill> skill via reference\" phrase in each\n  `.claude/agents/<archetype>.md` description frontmatter.\n\n  Sec MF-7 defense-in-depth: `subagent_type` is normalized via\n  `strip().lower()` (case-fold mirrors `check_agent_spawn.py:204`\n  archetype-routing precedent), then validated POST-NORMALIZE\n  against `_ARCHETYPE_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z][a-z0-9\\\\-]{0,63}$` with\n  `.fullmatch`). A raw-length pre-bound (`len > 80`) caps\n  hot-path allocation. Rejected silently: slash, dot-traversal,\n  NUL, unicode, oversize, non-string. Uppercase is INTENTIONALLY\n  case-folded (NOT rejected) — matches Agent-tool emitter\n  flexibility for the routing layer.\n\n## Rotation\n\nNEW in Sprint 2: monthly rotation by size threshold.\n\nBefore writing, if `audit-log.jsonl` exists and its size > ROTATE_AT_BYTES\n(default 10 MB), rename to `audit-log-YYYY-MM.jsonl` (current month) and\nstart a fresh file. If the monthly file already exists (second rotation\nin the same month), append `-1`, `-2`, etc.\n\nThe rotation rename happens UNDER the lock so a concurrent writer can't\nappend to a file that's about to be moved.\n\n## Safety properties\n\n1. Fail-open: any exception writes a breadcrumb to `audit-log.errors`\n   and exits 0. The user's session MUST NOT be blocked by this hook.\n2. Silent on stdout: composable with the reminder hook.\n3. Env-var overrides (`CEO_AUDIT_LOG_*`) for testability.\n4. Redaction via `_lib.redact` (property-tested).\n5. Locking via `_lib.filelock` (fcntl.flock).\n\n## Decomposition candidates\n\nThis module has accreted ~7 responsibilities across PLAN-019..PLAN-079.\nTracked decomposition targets for PLAN-085+ readers (NO extraction in\nPLAN-087 — doc-only surface; per `F-A-CR-D0016` P2 + PLAN-084 evolution\nroadmap):\n\n- **Path A — `extract_skill()` extraction.** Lines for the 3-path\n  matrix (Format-A inline / Format-B reference / Format-C ``## SKILL\n  CONTENT`` block) plus Path D canonical archetype map are a\n  self-contained extraction target. Candidate destination:\n  `_lib/skill_extract.py` (already exists as the standalone module\n  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` — the in-hook copy duplicates\n  logic kept inline so audit-log emit covers the dispatch hot path\n  without subprocess fork). Extraction would centralize the regex\n  contract; trade-off is per-spawn import cost.\n- **Path B — `usage_metadata` / `cache_coverage_bps` derivation.** The\n  v2.7 / v2.8 schema bump logic (lines ~15-43 in this docstring) is\n  arithmetic on `tool_response`. Candidate destination:\n  `_lib/usage_metadata.py` (mirrors `_lib/tokens.py` adapter pattern).\n- **Path C — HMAC chain integration.** The audit-chain HMAC writer\n  is currently invoked from this hook's main path. Candidate\n  destination: `_lib/audit_hmac.py` (already exists as the HMAC\n  verifier — the writer-side wrapper would mirror the\n  ``verify_chain()`` API). Extraction unblocks the two-writer\n  asymmetry surfaced as PLAN-084 finding C.1.\n- **Path D — Orchestrator split.** The PostToolUse dispatch logic\n  (rotation + redaction + emit + HMAC + breadcrumb fallback) is the\n  remaining \"orchestrator\" after Paths A/B/C peel off. Candidate\n  destination: keep `audit_log.py` as a ~150-line thin shim that\n  delegates to the four `_lib/*` modules.\n\nEach Path is sized to one PLAN-08x phase; extraction order is\nA → C → B → D (Path C unblocks the two-writer fix, so it lands\nahead of B/D).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport getpass\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport unicodedata\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n\n# Make `.claude/hooks/` importable so `_lib` resolves.\n_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n\nfrom _lib import contract as _contract  # noqa: E402\nfrom _lib import payload as _payload  # noqa: E402  (response_kind helper)\nfrom _lib import redact as _redact  # noqa: E402\nfrom _lib import tokens as _tokens  # noqa: E402  (PLAN-006 Phase 5b / ADR-016)\nfrom _lib.adapters import claude as _claude_adapter  # noqa: E402\nfrom _lib.filelock import FileLock, FileLockTimeout  # noqa: E402\ntry:\n    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402  # PLAN-182 W1 single resolver\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover — partial upgrade: hook stays FAIL-OPEN (rail r1 P1-4)\n    _rp = None  # type: ignore[assignment]\n\n\ndef _rp_state_dir():\n    \"\"\"Resolver com fallback de partial-upgrade (arquivo novo ausente).\n\n    Fail-open: o hook NUNCA crasha por falta do resolvedor; degrada ao\n    comportamento legado com aviso em stderr.\n    \"\"\"\n    if _rp is not None:\n        return _rp.runtime_state_dir()\n    import sys as _s  # pragma: no cover — partial-upgrade fallback\n    _s.stderr.write(\"# hook: _lib/runtime_paths ausente — fallback legado (partial upgrade)\\n\")  # pragma: no cover\n    from pathlib import Path as _P  # pragma: no cover\n    import os as _o  # pragma: no cover\n    _h = _o.environ.get(\"HOME\") or str(_P.home())  # pragma: no cover\n    return _P(_h) / \".claude\" / \"projects\" / \"ceo-orchestration\"  # rp-allow: partial-upgrade-fallback  # pragma: no cover\n\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Constants\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# Default rotation threshold: 10 MB. Overridable via CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES.\nDEFAULT_ROTATE_AT_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n\n# PLAN-065 Phase 1 — Sec MF-7 input bounds.\n# Cap inputs at 1 MiB to keep the regex engine in linear-time territory.\n# Plans / prompts beyond this size are extreme outliers; rejecting them is\n# preferred over feeding pathological input to the regex engine.\n_MAX_INPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024  # 1 MiB hard cap\n_MAX_INPUT_BYTES = _MAX_INPUT_CHARS\n\n# Skill-name max length (PLAN-065 §4.1 fixture spec — 256-char cap).\n_MAX_SKILL_NAME_CHARS = 256\n\n# Allowed skill-name character class — ``[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]*`` anchored.\n# Used as defense-in-depth re-validation post-extract.\n_SKILL_NAME_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]*$\")\n\n# PLAN-065 Phase 1 — 3-path SKILL extraction matrix.\n#\n# Path A — Format-A inline. Line-anchored ``^SKILL: <name>$``. Bounded\n# {0,255} quantifier on the captured group, no nested unbounded alternation\n# (ReDoS-safe). Mirrors the validated grammar in extract-skill.py:_PATH_A_RE.\n_SKILL_PATH_A_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?m)^SKILL:[ \\t]+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,255})\\s*$\",\n)\n\n# Path B — Format-B reference (mitigated dispatch + SKILL REFERENCE default).\n#   @.claude/skills/core/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>\n#   @.claude/skills/frontend/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>\n#   @.claude/skills/domains/<domain>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>\n# Captured group is the skill <name> path-segment, not the domain.\n_SKILL_PATH_B_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?m)^@\\.claude/skills/\"\n    r\"(?:core|frontend|domains/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,63}/skills)\"\n    r\"/([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,255})/SKILL\\.md\"\n    r\"\\s+sha256=[0-9a-f]{64}\\s*$\",\n)\n\n# Path C — `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Used when neither Format-A\n# nor Format-B was emitted (legacy / third-party adapter surface). The block\n# heading has a sibling `SKILL LOADED: <name>` annotation.\n_SKILL_PATH_C_HEADER_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?m)^##[ \\t]+SKILL[ \\t]+CONTENT\\b\",\n)\n_SKILL_PATH_C_LOADED_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?m)^SKILL[ \\t]+LOADED:[ \\t]+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\\-]{0,255})\\s*$\",\n)\n\n# PLAN-079 Path D — canonical archetype subagent_type → skill mapping.\n#\n# Sub-agent dispatches via ``Agent({subagent_type:\"<archetype>\"})`` load\n# their persona + skill via ``.claude/agents/<archetype>.md`` reference\n# per ADR-051 (PLAN-020). When the spawn prompt does NOT carry an\n# explicit Format-A/B/C SKILL envelope, Paths A-C all miss and the\n# pre-PLAN-079 behavior recorded ``skill=\"unknown\"``. This frozen map\n# closes the observability gap by mapping the 5 canonical archetypes\n# to their loaded skill name. Frozen baseline pattern (mirrors\n# ``_FROZEN_BASELINE`` in tier_policy/_constants.py) — no runtime I/O\n# against agent files; drift-detector test asserts the table matches\n# the \"Loads <skill> skill via reference\" phrase in each\n# ``.claude/agents/<archetype>.md`` description frontmatter.\n_ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL: Dict[str, str] = {\n    \"code-reviewer\": \"code-review-checklist\",\n    \"security-engineer\": \"security-and-auth\",\n    \"qa-architect\": \"testing-strategy\",\n    \"performance-engineer\": \"performance-engineering\",\n    \"devops\": \"devops-ci-cd\",\n    # PLAN-106 Wave B.2 (H3 fix) — additional archetypes recorded as\n    # `unknown` in 24h rolling because Path D lookup missed them. The\n    # canonical skill name on the right-hand side must match a real\n    # `.claude/skills/**/<name>/SKILL.md`. If the file is absent at\n    # adopter time the map still resolves the string; the downstream\n    # consumer is `audit_log.py:extract_skill()` Path D tail which\n    # records the string verbatim — no I/O.\n    \"identity-trust-architect\": \"identity-and-trust-architecture\",\n    \"incident-commander\": \"incident-management\",\n    \"llm-finops-architect\": \"llm-routing-and-finops\",\n    \"threat-detection-engineer\": \"security-and-auth\",\n}\n\n# Defense-in-depth charset for ``subagent_type`` AFTER `strip().lower()`\n# normalize (untrusted spawn-payload field). Bounded {0,63} quantifier —\n# no nested unbounded alternation (ReDoS-safe). Validated POST-NORMALIZE\n# via `.fullmatch` — uppercase input is case-folded BEFORE this check\n# (intentional, mirrors check_agent_spawn.py:204). Rejects (post-normalize):\n# dot-traversal `..`, slashes, NUL, unicode, oversize.\n_ARCHETYPE_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z][a-z0-9\\-]{0,63}$\")\n\n# Governance markers in the prompt\n_PROFILE_RE = re.compile(r\"^(## AGENT PROFILE|## PERSONA|PERSONA:)\", re.MULTILINE)\n_FILE_ASSIGNMENT_RE = re.compile(r\"^## FILE ASSIGNMENT\", re.MULTILINE)\n\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Path resolution\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n# PLAN-074 Wave 1c provenance — see docs/PLAN-086-adr-052-role-extension.md\n# Runtime declarations are split into installable, inspectable library files.\n# They execute once in this facade dictionary so private names, mutable globals\n# and monkeypatch seams retain the historical lookup behavior.\nfrom pathlib import Path as _FacadePath\n\n_PARTS = (\n    \"paths_skills\", \"entries_usage\", \"rotation_storage\", \"adapters_runtime\",\n)\n# Entry payload emits \"skill\" key via entries_usage.py\n_FACADE_DOC = __doc__\n\ndef _install_parts() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Execute ordered real source fragments in this module namespace.\"\"\"\n    namespace = globals()\n    directory = _FacadePath(__file__).resolve().parent / \"_lib\" / \"_audit_log_parts\"\n    for part_name in _PARTS:\n        part_path = directory / (part_name + \".py\")\n        source = part_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        exec(compile(source, str(part_path), \"exec\"), namespace, namespace)\n\n\n_install_parts()\n__doc__ = _FACADE_DOC\ndel _install_parts, _FacadePath, _FACADE_DOC\n","numLines":330,"startLine":1,"totalLines":330}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A6wABUA6HDAaKy94ac3jZh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
