{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AxkLpQfZYkmyPCbmoJVptd","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t        run: |\n151\t          set -euo pipefail\n152\t          python3 -m coverage run --rcfile=.coveragerc \\\n153\t            -m pytest .claude/sidecars/c5-dev-tools/hypothesis/tests -q --tb=short\n154\t\n155\t      - name: Combine parallel coverage + JSON export\n156\t        run: |\n157\t          set -euo pipefail\n158\t          python3 -m coverage combine --rcfile=.coveragerc\n159\t          python3 -m coverage json --rcfile=.coveragerc --ignore-errors -o coverage.json\n160\t\n161\t      - name: PLAN-093 parse-coverage gate (advisory — Wave A.5 kill-switch)\n162\t        # CEO_BRANCH_COVERAGE_ENFORCING=0 keeps this step advisory until a\n163\t        # future coverage-uplift sprint raises the baseline past 86%/85%.\n164\t        env:\n165\t          CEO_BRANCH_COVERAGE_ENFORCING: \"0\"\n166\t        run: |\n167\t          python3 .github/scripts/parse-coverage.py \\\n168\t            --branch-min 86 --line-min 85 \\\n169\t            --baseline-md .claude/plans/PLAN-093/wave-a-coverage-baseline.md \\\n170\t            --max-drop 2.0\n171\t\n172\t      - name: ADR-139 Tier-1 per-module coverage gate (ENFORCING)\n173\t        # PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-coverage-doctrine-reconcile (S157) / ADR-139.\n174\t        # Per-module enforcing gate at 86% for the modules MEASURED ≥86% under\n175\t        # subprocess capture (S157). check_agent_spawn.py stays ADVISORY (real\n176\t        # gaps in fail-open except branches + decide() core; uplift owner =\n177\t        # follow-on plan) and is intentionally NOT in this list. A module is\n178\t        # promoted here the moment it crosses 86% — no ceremony beyond the edit\n179\t        # (no-silent-LOWER clause: removals require an ADR-139 amendment).\n180\t        # Kill-switch: CEO_TIER1_COVERAGE_ENFORCING=0 (advisory).\n181\t        run: |\n182\t          set -euo pipefail\n183\t          python3 .github/scripts/parse-coverage.py \\\n184\t            --tier1-modules 'check_bash_safety.py,check_read_injection.py,check_canonical_edit.py,check_output_secrets.py,audit_log.py' \\\n185\t            --tier1-min 86\n186\t\n187\t      - name: Coverage report (text, enforcing repo-wide --fail-under line floor)\n188\t        run: |\n189\t          set -euo pipefail\n190\t          # PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-coverage-doctrine-reconcile (S157) / ADR-139:\n191\t          # the repo-wide line floor is an HONEST measured value under\n192\t          # subprocess capture, not the aspirational 86%. The real per-module\n193\t          # enforcement is the Tier-1 gate above; this repo-wide floor is a\n194\t          # belt-and-braces guard against a broad regression. The omit-list\n195\t          # (.claude/plans/* staging copies) lives in .coveragerc. CI TOTAL\n196\t          # measured 69.75% at S157 (hooks subprocess-captured; scripts in-\n197\t          # process only — script subprocess-capture is deferred follow-up\n198\t          # work, see ADR-139). Floor set ~2.75pp below as margin. This is the\n199\t          # belt, NOT the gate — the Tier-1 per-module 86% gate above is the\n200\t          # real enforcement. Raise as the script-capture + agent_spawn uplift\n201\t          # land (DYN-TEST-1 carries forward).\n202\t          python3 -m coverage report --rcfile=.coveragerc --skip-empty \\\n203\t            --fail-under=67 | tee coverage-text.txt\n204\t\n205\t      - name: Branch coverage advisory baseline (non-enforcing, F-03-03)\n206\t        # PLAN-045 F-03-03: branch coverage is measured (via --branch in\n207\t        # the run steps above) and reported here as an advisory baseline.\n208\t        # Output flows to coverage-branch-text.txt + GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n209\t        # Does NOT gate the build — the enforcing gate above is line-only"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"178172ab-278a-4318-ba3b-1534bf22937a","uuid":"f62ff496-bf5c-4758-b380-cdcf955e9b50"