bash_safety.py,check_read_injection.py,check_canonical_edit.py,check_output_secrets.py,audit_log.py' \\\n            --tier1-min 86\n\n      - name: Coverage report (text, enforcing repo-wide --fail-under line floor)\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          # PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-coverage-doctrine-reconcile (S157) / ADR-139:\n          # the repo-wide line floor is an HONEST measured value under\n          # subprocess capture, not the aspirational 86%. The real per-module\n          # enforcement is the Tier-1 gate above; this repo-wide floor is a\n          # belt-and-braces guard against a broad regression. The omit-list\n          # (.claude/plans/* staging copies) lives in .coveragerc. CI TOTAL\n          # measured 69.75% at S157 (hooks subprocess-captured; scripts in-\n          # process only — script subprocess-capture is deferred follow-up\n          # work, see ADR-139). Floor set ~2.75pp below as margin. This is the\n          # belt, NOT the gate — the Tier-1 per-module 86% gate above is the\n          # real enforcement. Raise as the script-capture + agent_spawn uplift\n          # land (DYN-TEST-1 carries forward).\n          python3 -m coverage report --rcfile=.coveragerc --skip-empty \\\n            --fail-under=67 | tee coverage-text.txt\n\n      - name: Branch coverage advisory baseline (non-enforcing, F-03-03)\n        # PLAN-045 F-03-03: branch coverage is measured (via --branch in\n        # the run steps above) and reported here as an advisory baseline.\n        # Output flows to coverage-branch-text.txt + GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n        # Does NOT gate the build — the enforcing gate above is line-only","numLines":60,"startLine":150,"totalLines":267}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AxkLpQfZYkmyPCbmoJVptd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
