tches 125 -> 222.\n  - _match_segments (:376-389) lets ** match zero segments, so files directly inside each package are kernel. Matching runs on lower-cased paths (:418, :434).\n  - The comment claims check out against the tree:\n    - plan_paths is imported by check_plan_edit.py:94 and policy_preprocessors.py:40;\n    - model_currency.is_veto_floor_model is called by agent_frontmatter.py:259 and escalation_signals.py:126, both kernel;\n    - cli_currency is imported by check_pair_rail.py:21 and _pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:3;\n    - bash_indirect_guard is imported at posture_scan.py:571, and bash_indirect_telemetry at decisions_cli.py:169;\n    - adapters/__init__.py:293 imports .live.claude_batch lazily.\n  - All seven facades were already kernel rows (:93, :94, :101, :105, :203, :204, :223).\n- Condition 7: both entry points keep their paths and registrations, and the logic moved into _lib modules.\n  - Removed names that resolve again: every top-level name the diff removes from check_agent_spawn.py (model routing, advisories, prompt rules, FILE ASSIGNMENT, skill reference, GOAP outcome, _BLOCK_REASON_MARKERS, main) is back in a part's __all__.\n  - Name lookup and patch points: the parts are bound to the facade's globals, so a monkeypatched facade name is still seen. _resolve_task_route's global writes land on the facade, and Path(__file__) still resolves to the facade.\n  - Fresh state: deepcopy gives each import its own _FRONTMATTER_MODEL_CACHE.\n  - No name clashes: no part's __all__ overwrites a name the facade defines.\n  - Faithful move: the audit_log parts match the removed text, including the condition-67 single-FileLock append_entry and the symlink/uid refusals.\n- Condition 9 (no silent model change): _ADR_052_ROLE_TO_MODEL moved verbatim to entries_usage.py:347-384, with the same values as the removed base text. The /effort rejection (_EFFORT_TOKEN_RE) is unchanged.\n\nFAIL DIRECTION, WRITES, PYTHON\n- check_agent_spawn, infrastructure fault: a part t